  "Number": 17,
  "Question": "A mixture of \\(30\\) liters of paint is \\(25\\%\\) red tint, \\(30\\%\\) yellow tint and \\(45\\%\\) water. Five liters of yellow tint are added to the original mixture. What is the percent of yellow tint in the new mixture?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(25\\)",
    "B": "\\(35\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\)",
    "D": "\\(45\\)",
    "E": "\\(50\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Find the amount of yellow tint before calculating its new percentage. Initially, the mixture contains\n\\[\n0.30\\times30=9\n\\]\nliters of yellow tint. Adding \\(5\\) liters increases the yellow amount to \\(9+5=14\\) liters and the total mixture to \\(30+5=35\\) liters.\n\nThe new percentage must use this new total:\n\\[\n\\frac{14}{35}=0.40=40\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{40\\%}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
